{
  "name": "Send new SAM.gov contract opportunities to Slack daily",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send new SAM.gov contract opportunities to Slack daily\n\n### Who it's for\nSmall federal contractors and BD teams who check SAM.gov every morning and still miss notices.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Schedule** fires every morning at 7:00.\n2. **Run SAM.gov Opportunity Radar** calls the Apify Actor (run-sync-get-dataset-items). It returns only notices that are **new or amended** since the last run, filtered by NAICS, set-aside, agency and state.\n3. **Has notice?** stops quietly on days with nothing new.\n4. **Post to Slack** sends one message per notice: title, type, agency, NAICS, set-aside, due date, short description, SAM.gov link.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Get your Apify API token: Apify Console > Settings > API & Integrations.\n2. In *Run SAM.gov Opportunity Radar*, create a **Header Auth** credential: Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`. Never paste the token into the URL or body.\n3. Connect your **Slack** credential in *Post to Slack* and pick the channel.\n4. Run once manually, check the output, then activate.\n\n### Customize the input\nEdit the JSON body of *Run SAM.gov Opportunity Radar*: `naicsCodes`, `setAside` (e.g. SBA, 8A, SDVOSBC, WOSB), `state`, `keywords`. Keep `monitorName` the same between runs, because that's what makes it \"new only\".\n\n### Requirements\nApify account, pay per result: $0.01 per run + $0.004 per new or changed notice. No SAM.gov API key needed (official public extract); add your own key for real-time data.\nActor: https://apify.com/cce_partners/samgov-opportunity-radar\n\n### How to extend\nSwap Slack for Microsoft Teams, Gmail or Discord; add an IF on `setAside` or `responseDeadline`; change the schedule.",
        "height": 820,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "621f0aea-7a54-46be-9654-bfa5abcfaec6",
      "name": "Overview and setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -380
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Schedule\nChange the cron/interval here. Runs once per period; the Actor itself skips anything already sent.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 220,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "16698e26-2b09-47dc-958a-9cfe7015b62d",
      "name": "Step 1: Schedule",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Run SAM.gov Opportunity Radar on Apify\nPOST to run-sync-get-dataset-items with your filters in the JSON body. Auth: your Header Auth credential (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`). Timeout 300 s.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 280,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "00a1e8d0-a49a-49a1-91f7-3adefaed5ad6",
      "name": "Step 2: Run the Actor",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        180,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3. Filter and deliver to Slack\n*Has notice?* stops when there's nothing new. Then the results go to Slack. Set your own credential and target (sheet ID / channel) on the last node.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 600,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "f4ce8b8d-581e-460e-9761-60e194f73be0",
      "name": "Step 3: Deliver",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        460,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "days",
              "triggerAtHour": 7
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "7803a498-a6f6-4aa7-bea1-eecb0af4d5dd",
      "name": "Schedule",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
